{"author": "mlkaldunski", "body": "I am struggling with the finding that the suggested replacement term, nucleocytoplasmic carrier activity (GO:0140142), is marked as Not4Curation\n", "created_at": "2026-06-15T14:52:32Z", "key": "comment:4709189208", "type": "comment", "updated_at": "2026-06-15T14:52:32Z"}
{"author": "ValWood", "body": "I think this constraint should be relaxed. We don't always know if import/export.\nv", "created_at": "2026-06-15T16:28:14Z", "key": "comment:4710056644", "type": "comment", "updated_at": "2026-06-15T16:28:14Z"}
{"author": "ValWood", "body": "i.e if you only have family information (the families are a mixture of import and export, I don't think we can say for sure)", "created_at": "2026-06-15T16:31:59Z", "key": "comment:4710085590", "type": "comment", "updated_at": "2026-06-15T16:31:59Z"}
{"author": "pgaudet", "body": "Hi @mlkaldunski \n\nYou need to use a child, either \nGO:0005049 nuclear export signal receptor activity or GO:0061608 nuclear import signal receptor activity. \n\nSorry about the confusion. ", "created_at": "2026-06-17T11:54:14Z", "key": "comment:4729652711", "type": "comment", "updated_at": "2026-06-17T11:54:14Z"}
{"author": "mlkaldunski", "body": "Yes, I understood that, thank you. But in this paper the experiments are binding assays of purified components so it isn't answered whether it's export or import activity. I've chosen a different term and completed the edits. I was able to add a cytosol CC annotation so that's a plus.\n", "created_at": "2026-06-17T16:06:19Z", "key": "comment:4732626363", "type": "comment", "updated_at": "2026-06-17T16:06:19Z"}
